@startuml spliced-walk-quadratic-time
' ============================================================================
' HISTORICAL BEFORE-STATE (PathMap report, "The dissolved store") — the
' spliced event-hash path was Theta(depth^2) in TIME as well as Theta(depth)
' in STACK.  The dispatch site this diagram depicts was DELETED with the
' InternedEPathMap store (SS-Y6, c0385b79): `contains_par` is constant-false,
' the spliced emitter is unreachable, and the surviving branch is the
' trampolined depth-flat `cold_encode`.  Retained as the measured
' before-mechanism of a before→after result, not as a live path.
'
' Diagram type: a SEQUENCE DIAGRAM with an explicit per-level repetition frame.
' Chosen because the quadratic cost is a fact about CALL MULTIPLICITY over
' nesting levels — `contains_par` is re-invoked once per level and each
' invocation descends the WHOLE remaining subtree.  A sequence diagram is the
' only type that makes "once per level, each descending everything" legible;
' a structure diagram would show the term but not the repetition.
'
' Colour convention — the report's Appendix E.3 mapping:
'   RED    #C62828 native stack / the sloped path
'   PURPLE #6A1B9A wire bytes
'   GREEN  #2E7D32 the converted control
'   AMBER  #EF6C00 the absence proof that costs a full descent
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #455A64
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE

title <b>HISTORICAL — the spliced walk was <latex>\Theta(d^2)</latex> in TIME, not only <latex>\Theta(d)</latex> in STACK</b>\nThe site was deleted with its store (SS-Y6, c0385b79); the surviving branch is the flat cold encoder

participant "`hash_produce` /\n`hash_consume`" as H #ECEFF1
participant "`event_hash_bytes_<leg>`\n`models/src/rust/`\n`spliced_event_bytes.rs`" as L #FFCDD2
participant "**`contains_par`**\n<i>the ABSENCE PROOF</i>\n`spliced_event_bytes.rs:223`" as C #FFE082
participant "`direct` =\n`bincode::serialize`\n<i>derived, recursive</i>" as D #EF9A9A
participant "`emit_<leg>`\n<i>hand-written, recursive</i>" as E #E1BEE7
participant "★ `ColdStoreEncode::`\n`cold_encode`\n<i>trampolined, <latex>O(1)</latex> stack</i>" as CE #A5D6A7

H -> L : one call per produce / bind / consume

group#EF6C00 #FFF3E0 **for EACH of the <latex>d</latex> nesting levels** — this frame is the quadratic term
  L -> C : `contains_par(value)` — **ALWAYS RUN**
  activate C #FFE082
  C -> C : mutually recursive with\n`contains_expr` over `EList.ps: Vec<Par>`
  note right of C #FFE082
    ★★ **Absence cannot be proved early.** To answer *"is there a
    filled `EPathMap` cell anywhere below me?"* with **false**,
    `contains_par` must visit **every descendant**. There is no
    short circuit on the negative answer.
    <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> one FULL descent, once per level:
    <latex>\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{d}(d - i) = \frac{d(d-1)}{2} = \Theta(d^2)</latex>
  end note
  C --> L : `false` (95.43 % of terms) / `true`
  deactivate C
end

alt#C62828 **`false`** <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> direct — the 95.43 % case
  L -> D : `bincode::serialize(value)`
  activate D #EF9A9A
  D --> L : bytes
  deactivate D
  note right of D #FFCDD2
    **MEASURED: 3,040 B/level debug · 160 release**
  end note
else **`true`** <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> spliced
  L -> E : `emit_<leg>(value, out)`
  activate E #E1BEE7
  E --> L : bytes with cached `serde_bytes` spliced in
  deactivate E
  note right of E #FFCDD2
    **MEASURED: 1,008 B/level debug · 208 release**
  end note
end

L --> H : the event hash — **reaches consensus twice over**\n`deploy_log` <latex>\rightarrow</latex> `Body.deploys` <latex>\rightarrow</latex> **block hash**, and `ReplayRSpace::rig`

== ★ THE CONTROL, in the same binary, on the same ladder ==

H -> CE : the `*-cold` control
activate CE #A5D6A7
CE --> H : byte-identical bytes
deactivate CE
note right of CE #E8F5E9
  ★★ **The control reads 0.0 / 0.0 B/level** — so the slope above is the
  **leg's own**, not the harness's or the fixture's.
  <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> **The repair is nearly free.** `ColdStoreEncode` is
  ALREADY implemented for all three legs' root types — `Par`,
  `BindPattern`, `ListParWithRandom`, `TaggedContinuation`. The legs
  simply never started calling it: `direct()` is still
  `bincode::serialize`. The **channel** leg WAS routed (`00ff9187`);
  these three were not.
end note

note across #FFCDD2
  ⚠ **Why a `SIGSEGV` here is a consensus-liveness exposure, not a robustness nit.**
  A native-stack overflow in Rust faults on the guard page; the runtime prints
  `fatal runtime error: stack overflow` and calls `abort()` — **signal 6, shell status 134**.
  It is **not catchable**, it is **not a failed deploy**, and it takes the whole node process.
end note

legend bottom
  |= cell |= meaning |
  |<#FFE082>| the absence proof — a full descent per level, the <latex>\Theta(d^2)</latex> term |
  |<#EF9A9A>| the direct leg — derived `Serialize`, recursive |
  |<#E1BEE7>| the spliced leg — hand-written, recursive; **wire bytes** |
  |<#A5D6A7>| the CONVERTED control, already implemented and not yet called |
endlegend

@enduml
